    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-xs">
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-surface-soft border border-hairline">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-ink mb-1">1. Clausius-Clapeyron Phase Kinetics</h4>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
          The saturation relationship between steam temperature and jacket gauge pressure governs heat flux. At 50 PSI (345 kPa), saturated steam reaches 297.7°F (147.6°C). In an unvented vessel, temperature rises exponentially: <code class="font-mono bg-surface px-1 py-0.5 rounded">ln(P2/P1) = (ΔHvap/R)·(1/T1 - 1/T2)</code>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-surface-soft border border-hairline">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-ink mb-1">2. ASME Section VIII Choked Orifice Discharge</h4>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
          Under ASME Section VIII Div 1 § UG-125, relieving capacity must satisfy: <code class="font-mono bg-surface px-1 py-0.5 rounded">W = 51.5·K·A·P</code> (lbs/hr steam). If mineral scale deposits reduce effective orifice area <code class="font-mono bg-surface px-1 py-0.5 rounded">A</code> by 70%, pressure accumulates past 110% of MAWP, exceeding design yield limits.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-surface-soft border border-hairline">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-ink mb-1">3. Timoshenko Shell Vacuum Buckling</h4>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
          Steam volume collapses 1,600-fold upon cooling. The critical external buckling pressure of a thin hemispherical shell is: <code class="font-mono bg-surface px-1 py-0.5 rounded">Pcrit = 0.366·E·(t/R)²</code>. At -28 inHg vacuum, external 14.7 PSI atmospheric force exceeds buckling limits, instantly crushing the inner liner.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Technical Engineering Matrix Table -->
